 "notes": "Lower boundary of the solid red 'SN1987A (This work)' exclusion region in Fig. 3 (combinedBoundsPlot.png from the e-print), digitised by color segmentation with axis calibration from tick marks. This is the paper's updated SN 1987A gamma-ray decay bound from the SMM non-observation (223 s window, 25-100 MeV), including Primakoff and photon-coalescence production; it extends from m_a ~ 31 keV to ~287 MeV with a minimum g_agamma ~ 1.6e-12 GeV^-1 near 110 MeV. The traced curve is the outer edge of the plotted region, i.e. the 2-sigma contour (F_gamma < 1.19 cm^-2); the 3-sigma contour (F_gamma < 1.78 cm^-2, convention of earlier literature) lies ~10% higher in coupling. The excluded region is closed: it also has an upper boundary at g ~ 8e-11 GeV^-1 (overlapping other astrophysical bounds); only the lower (headline) boundary is reported here, with the right-hand closure of the region captured by the rising last points. The red dashed Fermi-LAT curve in the same figure is a future-SN sensitivity projection and was excluded. No dark-matter density assumption is involved (astrophysical SN bound, not rescaled).",
